{
  "id": "minimax-h3-prism-dmad-pdmd-int8-pack",
  "name": "Community — MiniMax H3 (PRISM DMAD PDMD int8)",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "author": "OliviaRossi (merge of Singularity v2 and 10Eros Max); Zhengming Yu et al. (DMAD), Zimo Wang et al. and Iwannapose (PDMD)",
  "nsfw": false,
  "description": "Model format: int8 ConvRot. Steps: 8 by default.\n\nOliviaRossi's PRISM DMAD PDMD in its full-size int8 file (18.9 GB): the same merge and the same cards as the PRISM DMAD PDMD pack, which ships her smaller W6A8 file. Her PRISM merge of Singularity v2 and 10Eros Max, with the DMAD and PDMD distillations built in. Text, image and reference to video from one file, with no LoRA to load and nothing to install. It downloads from Hugging Face, so no Civitai key is needed. Eight steps by default (euler, simple, shift 12/3, no CFG); the slider covers four to ten. In our 2026-11-15 bake the two files gave the same composition, motion and camera on all seven prompts, with only small detail differences; this one is about 10% slower. Pick this pack if you have the memory and want the author's full-size weights. In reference to video the person stays recognisable, but a close-up picture of an object in its setting does not bring the setting with it: give it a wide picture of the whole place. Works with the app's Faster Attention toggle.",
  "tags": [
    "8-Step",
    "I2V",
    "Local",
    "Merge",
    "MiniMax H3",
    "R2V",
    "T2V",
    "Video"
  ],
