          "notes": "ONE checkpoint serves all three presets (18.9 GB int8 ConvRot, from Hugging Face, no key). Same merge as the PRISM DMAD PDMD pack, which ships the author's 14.8 GB W6A8 file; in our 2026-11-15 bake the two gave the same pictures, and this one ran about 10% slower (69-81 s against 62-73 s engine-direct over 36 clips, RTX 4070 Ti 12 GB, 864x480, 5 s). Eight steps by default, euler/simple, sigma shift 12.0 video / 3.0 audio, no CFG. The author recommends the beta57 scheduler, which needs RES4LYF; ComfyUI's beta scheduler at alpha 0.5 / beta 0.7 gave near-identical pictures to simple, so the cards use simple. The distillation is baked in, so there is no Turbo LoRA. MEASURED 2026-11-18 through the app (RTX 4070 Ti 12 GB, 864x480, 5 s, engine 0.45.0, faster attention on, eight steps): 75-77 s per text-to-video shot, 79-80 s per image-to-video shot and 79-83 s per reference shot (two seeds each). Spectrum step-skipping is deliberately NOT enabled: it garbled a spoken line on other distilled H3 checkpoints."
